# Safe environment-variable template for the reported Supabase setup.
# IMPORTANT: These names are examples only until matched against actual source code.
# Use only variable names the application code really reads; do not create a second naming scheme.
# Fill local values on your machine only. Never commit a real .env file or credentials.

# Server-side or tooling examples (only if referenced by code):
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLISHABLE-OR-ANON-KEY

# Vite/browser examples (only if the project actually uses Vite and these names):
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-PUBLISHABLE-OR-ANON-KEY

# SECURITY:
# - Browser-visible VITE_* values are public. Only a publishable/anon key may be exposed,
#   and only when the database is protected by correctly tested RLS/grants.
# - NEVER place a Supabase service_role key, database password, private token or secret in
#   frontend code, VITE_* variables, Git, screenshots, logs or this file.
# - Server-only secrets belong in ignored local configuration or an approved secret store.
# - These placeholders do not prove that the app uses any of these names or that Supabase
#   is configured. Verify client initialization and environment reads in source first.
